{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "game": "gi",
  "id": "rangi-nui-s-end",
  "name": "Rangi Nui's End",
  "sortId": 369203,
  "sourceUrl": "https://genshin-impact.fandom.com/wiki/Rangi_Nui%27s_End",
  "scrapedAt": "2026-09-06T11:27:03.023Z",
  "volumes": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "volumeKey": "vol-1",
      "label": "Vol. 1",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Rangi Nui's End is my hometown,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And whenever I recall my ancestral lands,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The morning sun shines over Rangi Nui,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Looking out over Waiata, the spring of flowing song,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Looking down upon Te Pahau, the wind-whiskered valley,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Looking across Poheka, the land of abundance,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Such are the lands of my grandparents,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Such is Rangi Nui's End."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-9371bead72ecdb1c"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I will journey to visit my ancestral home,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "On the twenty-fifth night, when the eels begin their dance,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "From Ohauiti shall I set forth, where the wind is gentle on the plains,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "To the waterfall where sharks do leap, to the shallow shoals,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "To Titiwha, those dazzling radiant depths,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Where I shall climb the mountain bathed in sunlight,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "To visit the long-slumbering master of mountain and stream,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "To explore the ancient dwelling place of the long-forgotten pygmies,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Before descending, descending into the valley's deepest depths,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Down to Te Tahutama, where luminescent fish congregate,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Down to Aka-aka, where plants grow small and strange."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Down to Mahinini, where the dark currents flow soft yet sharp,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Then down to dark Uropi, the depths of the forest..."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-168a5d3a12f1a84d"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Wo-ho! Wo-ho!"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "These distant, far-off lands, the hometown of my grandparents,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "They were thrown down, destroyed by disaster and violence, like collapsing mountains and raging wildfires..."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "My ancestors once lived in prosperity and peace, yet were plunged into famine and exile,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "My heart cries out for them, I mourn their tragic fate,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Like unquenchable flame roiling beneath spring waters, so profound a resentment, so deep a sorrow!"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Ever shall I wander along that never-ending wellspring of sighs,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And I shall come to fields of mottled green — that my ancestors called Kahotea."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And like the ancient dragons, soar effortlessly to the mountains where chants abound..."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The lost envoys of the heavens built there a city of gold and stone,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "But it was destroyed when raging flame fell from the heavens, the fury of the ancient sovereign."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Wo-ho! Wo-ho!"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-3c296602dc69727d"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And so I wander on, to Poheka, the land of abundance,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "There Rangi Nui once stood upright between heaven and earth, so the ancestors say,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "For he was both a sage who spoke to the heavens, and a hero of the land,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Whose soul returned to the rising sun, whereupon the sky itself became Rangi Nui."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Then, I shall head from the land of abundance to the distant shore,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And on a shore overgrown with tendrils, conclude my final journey."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-2da43dfd77e33816"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I once climbed the lonely, desolate volcano,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I have seen countless hot springs with my own eyes,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And I shall head to the other side of the dark currents,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "To seek the ferryman, who rows a dugout canoe and wears a gold-feathered crown,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And when at last I see that circlet, glimmering in gold,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Then shall I again reunite with my kin in the garden of Hairinei,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The birthplace of the forgotten sovereign of humans,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And I shall gather my tribespeople and friends, and we shall go there together."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-abdbb8019c190e39"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
